IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `qcat-dates`
IMPORT `qcat-applicant`

-- Queensland Civil and Administrative Tribunal Act 2009 -- worked cases for the questions of an applicant
-- (qcat-applicant.l4) and the date helpers (qcat-dates.l4). Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited
-- text; none was copied from the encoding's output. Each assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not
-- about the law. The facts and dates are illustrative.
-- Day counts used: 14 days after 1 March 2027 is 15 March 2027; 28 days after 1 March 2027 is 29 March 2027; 28 days
-- after 5 March 2027 is 2 April 2027; 28 days after 20 March 2027 is 17 April 2027; 28 days after 2 April 2027 is 30
-- April 2027; 28 days after 1 May 2027 is 29 May 2027; 28 days after 15 May 2027 is 12 June 2027; 28 days after 7 June
-- 2027 is 5 July 2027; 28 days after 10 February 2027 is 10 March 2027, and after 10 February 2028 (a leap year) 9 March
-- 2028; 28 days after 20 April 2027 is 18 May 2027; 45 days after 1 March 2027 is 15 April 2027; 7 days after 3 May 2027
-- is 10 May 2027; 21 days after 20 December 2027 is 10 January 2028; 14 days after 31 December 2027 is 14 January 2028;
-- 14 days after 10 March 2027 is 24 March 2027; 12 years after 15 June 2027 is 15 June 2039, after 29 February 2028 is
-- 29 February 2040, and after 29 February 2088 is 28 February 2100 (2100 is not a leap year).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `cases`

`d` MEANS `the calendar date`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `the date helpers`
-- ===================================================================================================================

#ASSERT `the day` 14 `days after` (`d` 1 3 2027) EQUALS `d` 15 3 2027
#ASSERT `the day` 28 `days after` (`d` 10 2 2028) EQUALS `d` 9 3 2028
#ASSERT `the day` 28 `days after` (`d` 10 2 2027) EQUALS `d` 10 3 2027
#ASSERT `the day` 21 `days after` (`d` 20 12 2027) EQUALS `d` 10 1 2028
#ASSERT `the earlier of` (`d` 20 3 2027) `and` (`d` 2 4 2027) EQUALS `d` 20 3 2027
#ASSERT `the earlier of` (`d` 10 4 2027) `and` (`d` 2 4 2027) EQUALS `d` 2 4 2027
#ASSERT `the date` 12 `years after` (`d` 15 6 2027) EQUALS `d` 15 6 2039
#ASSERT `the date` 12 `years after` (`d` 29 2 2088) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2100
#ASSERT `the days from` (`d` 1 3 2027) `to` (`d` 29 3 2027) EQUALS 28

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `minor civil disputes`
-- ===================================================================================================================

`mcd yes` MEANS `yes: it is a minor civil dispute (schedule 3, paragraph 1), and you may apply to the tribunal to hear and decide it (ss 11, 12(1))`
`mcd if limited` MEANS `yes, but only if you agree to limit your claim to $25,000: applying to the tribunal to deal with it as a minor civil dispute limits it, and you give up the rest (s 12(2), (3))`
`mcd not a kind` MEANS `no: not one of the kinds of claim in schedule 3, paragraph 1 (definition of minor civil dispute)`
`mcd enabling` MEANS `no: an enabling Act gives the tribunal jurisdiction over this debt claim and does not expressly say it is a minor civil dispute (schedule 3, paragraph 2)`
`mcd fair work` MEANS `no: a claim under the Fair Work Act 2009 (Cwlth), section 539 is not a minor civil dispute (schedule 3, paragraph 4)`
`mcd fair trading` MEANS `no: a claim in a proceeding to which the Fair Trading Act 1989, section 50A applies is not a minor civil dispute (schedule 3, paragraph 3)`
`mcd not consumer or trader` MEANS `no: only the consumer (under a contract between a consumer and a trader) or a trader (under a contract between traders) may bring this contract claim as a minor civil dispute (schedule 3, paragraph 1(b); s 12(1), (4)(b), (c))`
`mcd not relevant person` MEANS `no: you are not the person who may apply to the tribunal for this kind of claim (s 12(1), (4))`

`debt` MEANS `a claim to recover a debt or liquidated demand of money`
`contract` MEANS `a claim arising out of a contract for goods or services, or a lease of a dwelling`
`vehicle` MEANS `a claim for damage to property caused by, or arising out of the use of, a vehicle`
`tenancy` MEANS `a tenancy matter under the Residential Tenancies and Rooming Accommodation Act 2008`
`fences` MEANS `a dividing fences or trees dispute under the Neighbourhood Disputes (Dividing Fences and Trees) Act 2011, chapter 2`
`pool` MEANS `a pool barrier matter under the Building Act 1975, chapter 8, part 2A`

-- A debt: up to $25,000 (the definition says "up to"), then the s 12(2) limit; paragraphs 2 and 4; s 12(4)(a).
#ASSERT `Is my claim a minor civil dispute` `debt` 25000 TRUE FALSE `something else` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `mcd yes`
#ASSERT `Is my claim a minor civil dispute` `debt` 25001 TRUE FALSE `something else` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `mcd if limited`
#ASSERT `Is my claim a minor civil dispute` `debt` 800 TRUE FALSE `something else` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `mcd yes`
#ASSERT `Is my claim a minor civil dispute` `debt` 800 TRUE FALSE `something else` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `mcd enabling`
#ASSERT `Is my claim a minor civil dispute` `debt` 800 TRUE FALSE `something else` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `mcd fair work`
#ASSERT `Is my claim a minor civil dispute` `debt` 800 FALSE FALSE `something else` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `mcd not relevant person`

-- A contract: a consumer against a trader, at, below and over the limit.
#ASSERT `Is my claim a minor civil dispute` `contract` 10000 FALSE TRUE `goods I bought or hired` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `mcd yes`
#ASSERT `Is my claim a minor civil dispute` `contract` 25000 FALSE TRUE `services supplied to me for a fee or reward` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `mcd yes`
#ASSERT `Is my claim a minor civil dispute` `contract` 30000 FALSE TRUE `goods I bought or hired` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `mcd if limited`
-- A tenant against a landlord who is not otherwise in business: the landlord is a trader (schedule 3, trader 1(b)).
#ASSERT `Is my claim a minor civil dispute` `contract` 3000 FALSE TRUE `premises let to me as a dwelling` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `mcd yes`
-- Bought for my business, and I am not a trader: not a consumer, not 2 traders.
#ASSERT `Is my claim a minor civil dispute` `contract` 3000 FALSE TRUE `goods I bought or hired` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `mcd not consumer or trader`
-- Two traders: either may apply (s 12(4)(c)); a company that is a trader too.
#ASSERT `Is my claim a minor civil dispute` `contract` 3000 FALSE TRUE `goods I bought or hired` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `mcd yes`
#ASSERT `Is my claim a minor civil dispute` `contract` 3000 FALSE FALSE `something else` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `mcd yes`
-- A trader suing a consumer on the contract: only the consumer may bring a 1(b) claim (finding 1).
#ASSERT `Is my claim a minor civil dispute` `contract` 3000 FALSE FALSE `something else` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `mcd not consumer or trader`
-- A professional outside trade or commerce is not a trader (trader 2).
#ASSERT `Is my claim a minor civil dispute` `contract` 3000 FALSE TRUE `services supplied to me for a fee or reward` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `mcd not consumer or trader`
-- Something else under the contract: not a consumer.
#ASSERT `Is my claim a minor civil dispute` `contract` 3000 FALSE TRUE `something else` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `mcd not consumer or trader`
-- A company is not a consumer.
#ASSERT `Is my claim a minor civil dispute` `contract` 3000 FALSE FALSE `goods I bought or hired` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `mcd not consumer or trader`
-- Fair Trading Act s 50A (paragraph 3).
#ASSERT `Is my claim a minor civil dispute` `contract` 3000 FALSE TRUE `goods I bought or hired` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `mcd fair trading`

-- Vehicle damage, tenancy, fences, pool barriers, and another kind.
#ASSERT `Is my claim a minor civil dispute` `vehicle` 5000 TRUE FALSE `something else` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `mcd yes`
#ASSERT `Is my claim a minor civil dispute` `vehicle` 40000 TRUE FALSE `something else` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `mcd if limited`
#ASSERT `Is my claim a minor civil dispute` `vehicle` 5000 FALSE FALSE `something else` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `mcd not relevant person`
#ASSERT `Is my claim a minor civil dispute` `tenancy` 100000 TRUE FALSE `something else` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `mcd yes`
#ASSERT `Is my claim a minor civil dispute` `tenancy` 100 FALSE FALSE `something else` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `mcd not relevant person`
#ASSERT `Is my claim a minor civil dispute` `fences` 25000 TRUE FALSE `something else` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `mcd yes`
#ASSERT `Is my claim a minor civil dispute` `fences` 26000 TRUE FALSE `something else` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `mcd if limited`
#ASSERT `Is my claim a minor civil dispute` `pool` 90000 TRUE FALSE `something else` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `mcd yes`
#ASSERT `Is my claim a minor civil dispute` `another kind of claim` 100 TRUE TRUE `goods I bought or hired` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `mcd not a kind`

-- s 13(3)-(5): the cap.
#ASSERT `What is the most the tribunal can order in my minor civil dispute` `debt` 10000 EQUALS JUST 10000
#ASSERT `What is the most the tribunal can order in my minor civil dispute` `debt` 25000 EQUALS JUST 25000
#ASSERT `What is the most the tribunal can order in my minor civil dispute` `contract` 25001 EQUALS JUST 25000
#ASSERT `What is the most the tribunal can order in my minor civil dispute` `tenancy` 30000 EQUALS JUST 25000
#ASSERT `What is the most the tribunal can order in my minor civil dispute` `pool` 30000 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `What is the most the tribunal can order in my minor civil dispute` `another kind of claim` 300 EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 14: interest.
#ASSERT `Can the tribunal add interest to my minor civil dispute award` `debt` FALSE EQUALS `the tribunal may include interest, at the rate it considers appropriate, for all or part of the amount and all or part of the period from when the dispute arose to its order, but not interest on interest (s 14(3), (4))`
#ASSERT `Can the tribunal add interest to my minor civil dispute award` `debt` TRUE EQUALS `s 14 does not apply: interest is payable on this debt as of right, under an agreement or otherwise; it is not counted toward the $25,000 limit (ss 11A(1)(a), 13(5), 14(2))`
#ASSERT `Can the tribunal add interest to my minor civil dispute award` `vehicle` FALSE EQUALS `s 14 does not apply: it reaches only a minor civil dispute to recover a debt or liquidated demand of money (s 14(1))`

