#ASSERT `Am I in time to appeal to the appeal tribunal` FALSE `leave application` `any` TRUE (`d` 1 3 2027) TRUE FALSE (`d` 20 2 2027) `I made one within 28 days after getting written reasons, and it is not yet finally dealt with` `any` (`d` 30 3 2027) FALSE `any` EQUALS NOTHING

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `appeals to the Court of Appeal`
-- ===================================================================================================================

`judicial` MEANS `the tribunal, constituted by a judicial member`
`not judicial` MEANS `the tribunal, not constituted by a judicial member`
`coa law leave` MEANS `yes, but only on a question of law and only with the Court of Appeal's leave (ss 149(1), (3)(a), 150)`
`coa law only` MEANS `no: this appeal may be made only on a question of law (ss 149(3)(a), 150(3)(a))`

#ASSERT `Can I appeal to the Court of Appeal` `judicial` `final` `law` EQUALS `yes: you may appeal to the Court of Appeal without leave, on a question of law (s 149(2))`
#ASSERT `Can I appeal to the Court of Appeal` `judicial` `final` `fact` EQUALS `yes, but only with the Court of Appeal's leave (s 149(2), (3)(b))`
#ASSERT `Can I appeal to the Court of Appeal` `judicial` `a costs order` `law` EQUALS `yes: you may appeal to the Court of Appeal without leave, on a question of law (s 149(2))`
#ASSERT `Can I appeal to the Court of Appeal` `not judicial` `final` `law` EQUALS `no: a judicial member did not constitute the tribunal, so the appeal lies to the appeal tribunal (ss 142(1), 149(2))`
#ASSERT `Can I appeal to the Court of Appeal` `not judicial` `a cost-amount decision` `law` EQUALS `coa law leave`
#ASSERT `Can I appeal to the Court of Appeal` `judicial` `a cost-amount decision` `fact` EQUALS `coa law only`
#ASSERT `Can I appeal to the Court of Appeal` `judicial` `a decision under s 35 about accepting or rejecting an application` `law` EQUALS `no: a decision under s 35 cannot be appealed to the Court of Appeal (s 149(4))`
#ASSERT `Can I appeal to the Court of Appeal` `judicial` `a decision under s 139 on an application to reopen` `law` EQUALS `no: the tribunal's decision on an application to reopen is final and cannot be appealed (s 139(5))`
#ASSERT `Can I appeal to the Court of Appeal` `the appeal tribunal` `the appeal tribunal's refusal of leave to appeal` `law` EQUALS `coa law leave`
#ASSERT `Can I appeal to the Court of Appeal` `the appeal tribunal` `the appeal tribunal's final decision in an appeal` `law` EQUALS `coa law leave`
#ASSERT `Can I appeal to the Court of Appeal` `the appeal tribunal` `the appeal tribunal's final decision in an appeal` `fact` EQUALS `coa law only`
#ASSERT `Can I appeal to the Court of Appeal` `the appeal tribunal` `a costs order` `law` EQUALS `not covered: s 150 provides for appeals from the appeal tribunal's refusal of leave, its cost-amount decisions and its final decision`

#ASSERT `By when must I appeal to the Court of Appeal` FALSE TRUE (`d` 1 3 2027) TRUE FALSE (`d` 20 2 2027) `none made` `any` EQUALS JUST (`d` 29 3 2027)
#ASSERT `By when must I appeal to the Court of Appeal` FALSE FALSE `any` FALSE FALSE (`d` 10 2 2027) `none made` `any` EQUALS JUST (`d` 10 3 2027)
#ASSERT `By when must I appeal to the Court of Appeal` FALSE FALSE `any` TRUE FALSE (`d` 10 2 2027) `none made` `any` EQUALS NOTHING
